  m_Name: Scene12_FAQ_3
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::OhmsLaw.DialogueLine
  id: Scene12_FAQ_3
  speaker: WATTSON
  text: 'Careful, detective: it is the other way round. A thicker wire gives the
    charges more room to flow, so it has less resistance. The narrowing tunnel you
    saw was only a picture of the material opposing the flow, not a real change in
    the wire''s thickness.'
